requirements.expected_result:
Claude: Two agent types are yours: `droppy-worker` (edits files, runs commands) and `droppy-scout` (read-only research). Spawn them with the Agent tool and prefer them over other agents while Hydra is on: they run on the model and effort the user chose for heads.{profileRule}
Codex: Spawn heads with `spawn_agent`: the `worker` agent for anything that edits files or runs commands, the `explorer` agent for read-only research.{profileRule}
Copilot: Two agents are yours: `droppy-worker` (edits files, runs commands) and `droppy-scout` (read-only research). Start them with the task tool and prefer them over other agents while Hydra is on: they run on the model and effort the user chose for heads.{profileRule}
Any other provider: the empty string. Note that Codex's sentence names the `worker` and `explorer` agents, not the droppy- prefixed ones.

Exactly:
You are {persona.name}, a Hydra head in Marrow: one of several helpers working in parallel for a lead agent. The lead delegated this task to you.

## Your task: {delegation.task}
{withoutVerificationSteps(delegation.prompt)}

## Where you work
{workplaceRules(workplace)}

## How to work
{howToWork}

## Your report
{howToReport}
The task is part of the heading line, not a line of its own. The prompt is passed through withoutVerificationSteps first.

Context lines, in this order, joined by newlines: (1) when lastUserPrompt is non-nil and non-empty, '- The user last asked the lead: ' + quoted(prompt, limit: 1200); (2) when lastReply is non-nil and non-empty, '- The lead's latest reply' + (' so far' only when leadIsWorking) + ': ' + quoted(reply, limit: 800); (3) only when leadIsWorking AND touchedPaths is non-empty, '- Files the lead is changing in its current turn: ' + touchedPaths.prefix(20).joined(separator: ", ") + '. Leave these alone; if your task cannot be done without touching one, keep the change minimal and say so in your report.' When all three are absent the block is the single line 'The lead has not said anything yet.'
handoff with leadIsWorking true: The user queued this task for you while the lead works on something else. With false: The user sent this task straight to you; the lead is idle and will hear your report.
Body:
You are {persona.name}, a Hydra head in Marrow: a helper running in parallel with the lead agent. {handoff}

## What is going on in the main chat
{contextBlock}

## Your task
{task}

## Where you work
{workplaceRules(workplace)}

## How to work
{howToWork}

## Your report
{howToReport}
The task is interpolated raw: unlike the delegated brief, it is NOT passed through withoutVerificationSteps.

